+## Notes checkpoint only for `/compact context` (2026-10-16)
+
+- User ask: stop recording notes before plain compaction; record only when the compact subcommand is `context`. The ask timed out unanswered, so the recommended defaults were taken and are NOT user-confirmed: (1) "context" means a new manual subcommand `/compact context`; (2) plain `/compact` under a live notebook takes the configured `compaction.methodOrder` summary path; (3) repository and verifiers only, no deployment.
+- Behavior: `/compact context` is the only manual path that runs the hidden `manual-compaction-notes-checkpoint` and then the notes-backed rollover. Plain `/compact`, `/compact soft|remote|snapcompact`, focus text and `internalGuidance` never checkpoint and never reach `#compactExperimentalContext`. `context` rejects focus text and, when the notebook is not live, rejects before `disconnectFromAgent()`/`abort()` so a running turn survives. Automatic compaction, child sessions and notebook-disabled sessions are unchanged.
+- Gate coupling: the strict save gate vetoed every `session_before_compact`, so a stale notebook would have blocked the new summary path. `SessionBeforeCompactEvent.notesBacked?: boolean` is emitted `true` at both notes-backed rollover sites and `false` at both summary sites; the gate skips only an explicit `false`. An absent marker still vetoes, so a new extension on an old runtime and an old extension on any runtime both stay fail-closed. Consequence of the old extension on the new runtime: plain `/compact` with a stale notebook is still vetoed until the extension mirror is redeployed.
+- Rejected: keeping plain `/compact` notes-backed without the checkpoint (the gate would veto it whenever the notebook is stale, so "don't record" would mean "refuse"); letting the gate pass every manual compaction (would also pass `/compact context`); inferring mode from `customInstructions` or idle state inside the hook (no reliable signal); a new `compaction.methodOrder` value `context` (no such method exists; widens the change); a new setting or patch family.
+- Behavior change for callers that pass no mode and previously received the notes-backed rollover under a live notebook: TUI/ACP slash `/compact`, RPC `compact` (no mode field, so RPC clients cannot request `context`), compact-first model switch (`selector-controller.ts`), loop-mode compact iterations, and extension/SDK `ctx.compact()` without options (extensions opt in with `{ mode: "context" }`). No installed local extension calls `compact`. These callers now summarize instead of rolling over.
+- Patch integration: `family-compaction-v18.10.1.patch` regenerated from the pinned prefix (family SHA-256 `4aae367192272590c86277dfe93e1e6f4d1535fea055adaa22d937cfab3d15c0`, candidate tree `366940414a5424afefa0c4f681b13ec0a27be8259bb47550813510fe92051bcd`). Superseded family, generated delta and baseline are pinned under `patches/.retired/10-16-18.10.1-compaction-pre-compact-context/`. The stock `dist/cli.js` bundle stays unmarked by design (source entrypoints execute under Bun, per PATCHES.md).
+- Verification: `verify-manual-notes-compaction.ts` 19/19 on the candidate tree and 16/19 failing on the pre-change installed runtime; `verify-context-notes-save-gate.ts` passes with nine mutation controls rejected (two new: marker ignored, absent marker treated as summary); `verify-context-notes-append-projection.ts` 14/14 unchanged; family oracle 26 families / 61 capabilities (zero-fuzz forward, reverse to pristine, identical second replay, read-only controller identification). An independent read-only reviewer re-ran the gates, enumerated all emit sites and callers, and returned approve with no findings. Evidence: `.notes-compact-context-smoke/`.
+- Verification gap found: the earlier manual-checkpoint harness never loaded the save gate (sessions with `restrictToolNames` ignore `additionalExtensionPaths`), so its "no repair turn" claim was not exercised against the real gate. The harness now injects the real gate through `preloadedPreparedExtensions`, and a marker-stripped control proves the gate is live. The automatic summary-path `notesBacked:false` site is verified by diff and grep only, not executed.
+- Not done: deployment, installed extension mirror `~/.omp/agent/extensions/context-notes-save-gate.ts`, live-provider smoke. Activation needs an immutable-release publish plus the extension mirror copy and a clean restart; no hot activation is claimed.
+
+### Five-question check
+
+1. Which manual command records notes first? Only `/compact context`.
+2. What does plain `/compact` do under a live notebook now? Summary compaction by `compaction.methodOrder`, with no checkpoint and no gate veto.
+3. What does an absent `notesBacked` marker mean to the gate? Notes-backed, so it vetoes while the notebook is stale.
+4. What happens on `/compact context` when the notebook is not live? An immediate rejection before the running turn is aborted.
+5. Is anything deployed? No; runtime release publish and the extension mirror copy are separate steps.
